IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ar62-nouns`
IMPORT `ar62-cross-references`

-- Row il-62. The controls hold, and the recorded facts about the finding are what NOTES.md says they are.
-- The finding itself is NOT asserted sound anywhere in this file: its three failing assertions are in ar62-tests-xrefs-red.l4.
-- Every expected value is written from the texts quoted in ar62-cross-references.l4 (the `ext:` and `src:` lines), not from the output of the module.

§ `Tests of the range the citing words name`

#ASSERT (`range: the words "(1) עד (5)" at the end of s 35(b)`)'s `the first paragraph named` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT (`range: the words "(1) עד (5)" at the end of s 35(b)`)'s `the last paragraph named` EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the number of paragraphs the range names` (`range: the words "(1) עד (5)" at the end of s 35(b)`) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the range names the paragraph` (`range: the words "(1) עד (5)" at the end of s 35(b)`) (`paragraph (5) of s 35(b)`)
#ASSERT `the range names the paragraph` (`range: the words "(1) עד (5)" at the end of s 35(b)`) (`paragraph (1) of s 35(b)`)

§ `Tests of the control: paragraphs (1) to (4) exist`

-- The consolidation prints text for each, prints none of them as deleted, and no instrument read by this row directs that any of them be deleted.
#ASSERT (`paragraph (1) of s 35(b)`)'s `the consolidation prints text for it`
#ASSERT (`paragraph (2) of s 35(b)`)'s `the consolidation prints text for it`
#ASSERT (`paragraph (3) of s 35(b)`)'s `the consolidation prints text for it`
#ASSERT (`paragraph (4) of s 35(b)`)'s `the consolidation prints text for it`
#ASSERT NOT (`paragraph (1) of s 35(b)`)'s `the consolidation prints it as deleted`
#ASSERT NOT (`paragraph (2) of s 35(b)`)'s `the consolidation prints it as deleted`
#ASSERT NOT (`paragraph (3) of s 35(b)`)'s `the consolidation prints it as deleted`
#ASSERT NOT (`paragraph (4) of s 35(b)`)'s `the consolidation prints it as deleted`
#ASSERT NOT (`paragraph (4) of s 35(b)`)'s `an instrument read by this row directs that it be deleted`
#ASSERT `the range names the paragraph` (`range: the words "(1) עד (5)" at the end of s 35(b)`) (`paragraph (4) of s 35(b)`)
-- Paragraph (4) is the last paragraph before the one printed as deleted, and it is not that one.
#ASSERT (`paragraph (4) of s 35(b)`)'s `its number` EQUALS 4
#ASSERT (`paragraph (4) of s 35(b)`)'s `the instrument that adds it` EQUALS "not read by this row"

§ `Tests of what the records say about paragraph (5)`

#ASSERT (`paragraph (5) of s 35(b)`)'s `its number` EQUALS 5
#ASSERT (`paragraph (5) of s 35(b)`)'s `the consolidation prints it as deleted`
#ASSERT NOT (`paragraph (5) of s 35(b)`)'s `the consolidation prints text for it`
#ASSERT (`paragraph (5) of s 35(b)`)'s `an instrument read by this row directs that it be deleted`
#ASSERT (`paragraph (5) of s 35(b)`)'s `the instrument that adds it` EQUALS "section 51(2) of Sefer HaChukim 1973, printed p. 89"
#ASSERT (`paragraph (5) of s 35(b)`)'s `the instrument that directs its deletion` EQUALS "section 86(3) of Sefer HaChukim 2556, printed p. 927"
-- Counting over the range: one paragraph printed as deleted and one directed deleted; the first four paragraphs alone would give none.
#ASSERT `the number of paragraphs the range names that the consolidation prints as deleted` (`range: the words "(1) עד (5)" at the end of s 35(b)`) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the number of paragraphs the range names that an instrument read by this row directs be deleted` (`range: the words "(1) עד (5)" at the end of s 35(b)`) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `one if the range names the paragraph and the consolidation prints it as deleted` (`range: the words "(1) עד (5)" at the end of s 35(b)`) (`paragraph (4) of s 35(b)`) EQUALS 0

§ `Tests of the date pairs`

-- Each Hebrew date printed with a Gregorian date gives that Gregorian date in the routine, and the printed pairs are the ones typed.
#ASSERT `the printed pair matches the routine` (`date pair: the footer of printed p. 89 of Sefer HaChukim 1973`)
#ASSERT `the printed pair matches the routine` (`date pair: the footer of printed p. 927 of Sefer HaChukim 2556`)
#ASSERT (`date pair: the footer of printed p. 89 of Sefer HaChukim 1973`)'s `the Hebrew date, transliterated` EQUALS "29 Tevet 5765"
#ASSERT (`date pair: the footer of printed p. 89 of Sefer HaChukim 1973`)'s `the Gregorian date printed with it` EQUALS Date 10 1 2005
#ASSERT (`date pair: the footer of printed p. 927 of Sefer HaChukim 2556`)'s `the Hebrew date, transliterated` EQUALS "17 Sivan 5776"
#ASSERT (`date pair: the footer of printed p. 927 of Sefer HaChukim 2556`)'s `the Gregorian date printed with it` EQUALS Date 23 6 2016
-- The instrument that adds paragraph (5) is issued before the one that directs its deletion.
#ASSERT (`date pair: the footer of printed p. 89 of Sefer HaChukim 1973`)'s `the Gregorian date printed with it` LESS THAN (`date pair: the footer of printed p. 927 of Sefer HaChukim 2556`)'s `the Gregorian date printed with it`

§ `Tests of what was read from where`

-- Limb (b) of the finding: the instruments were read from their page images; that the tail still reads so today is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY.
#ASSERT (`range: the words "(1) עד (5)" at the end of s 35(b)`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official instruments read from their page images; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
-- Limb (a): paragraph (5) was read from the official pages; that no later instrument touched it is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY. Paragraphs (1) to (4) were read from the consolidation only.
#ASSERT (`paragraph (5) of s 35(b)`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the official instruments read from their page images; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
#ASSERT (`paragraph (4) of s 35(b)`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
-- The two printed date pairs are the instruments' own words.
#ASSERT (`date pair: the footer of printed p. 89 of Sefer HaChukim 1973`)'s `the pair was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
#ASSERT (`date pair: the footer of printed p. 927 of Sefer HaChukim 2556`)'s `the pair was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
